# Copy to server/.env and fill in. Docker Compose reads it; `npm start` in server/ does too.

# Required. The shared secret both phones type once to join your household.
# Make it long: anyone who knows it can join.
HOUSEHOLD_CODE=

# Shown in the app. The admin command `household-name` changes it without a restart, and from then
# on its name wins over this one.
HOUSEHOLD_NAME=Our home

# Optional. Turns on the AI helper ("check my Japanese", "how do I say this?").
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5

# Your home time zone. A study day ends at 4 a.m. here; it decides the shared streak.
# TZ=America/Chicago

# Behind a reverse proxy (Caddy, nginx, Tailscale serve, …) set this to the address the proxy
# connects from, so rate limits see real client IPs: an IP, a CIDR range or "loopback", several
# comma-separated. Under Docker the proxy usually arrives from Docker's networks, 172.16.0.0/12.
# Avoid "true": it also believes X-Forwarded-For entries a client makes up.
# TRUST_PROXY=172.16.0.0/12

# LOG_LEVEL=info

# Only used outside Docker; docker-compose.yml pins these inside the container.
# Relative paths are from server/.
# PORT=8787
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# DATA_DIR=./data
# STATIC_DIR=../dist
